                <pb facs="0935" n="928" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg928"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8914: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-22T14:00:00+08:00">July 22, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 22—9:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>279. The following telegram has been received from the Consulate General at
                    Harbin.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“15, July 21, 3 p.m. Information here is that the Japanese Army in North
                        Manchuria is concentrated in greater strength than are reported on the
                        Soviet border. Russian mechanics in Harbin have been recruited recently in
                        some numbers by the Japanese Army for work near the Russian frontier”.</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Repeated to Tokyo, Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
